le":"Covering input and elementary estimates","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:552cdd7c5ba4019abe61c9792df1618157c781dbfba3a020de27cc7c291ec050","file":"preprints/Graph-Decompositions-at-the-Integral-Expectation-Threshold-October-5-2026/build/main.tex","line":185,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"a9ecabe90c0083832da5a0233969f9cf10aeee0faf70e1fd0fe1027dca540c3e","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Graph-Decompositions-at-the-Integral-Expectation-Threshold-October-5-2026/build/main.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:552cdd7c5ba4019abe61c9792df1618157c781dbfba3a020de27cc7c291ec050","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Graph-Decompositions-at-the-Integral-Expectation-Threshold-October-5-2026/build/main.tex#L185"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"{OpenAI26DC}}]\n\\label{thm:discrete}\nSet $K_0=2^{75}$. For every nonempty finite set $X$, every\n$r\\in(0,1)$, and every family $\\calD\\subseteq2^X$ with\n$\\mu_r(\\calD)\\geq1-1/K_0$, the family\n\\[\n \\mathcal E_{K_0}(\\calD)=\n \\{S\\subseteq X:S\\not\\subseteq D_1\\cup\\cdots\\cup D_{K_0}\n                   \\text{ for every }D_1,\\ldots,D_{K_0}\\in\\calD\\}\n\\]\nhas a cover of cost at most $1/2$ at the same parameter $r$.\nThe family $\\calD$ need not be monotone, and members of a tuple\nmay repeat."}
